WEBVTT

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:02.225
Lesson 8.2.

00:00:02.225 --> 00:00:03.930
The DeFi risk framework.

00:00:03.930 --> 00:00:06.055
By the end of this lesson, you'll be

00:00:06.055 --> 00:00:08.409
able to keep a risk register that scores

00:00:08.409 --> 00:00:11.050
every position's risks and names the response.

00:00:12.350 --> 00:00:13.640
Here's the plan.

00:00:13.640 --> 00:00:15.325
First, the key ideas.

00:00:15.325 --> 00:00:18.040
Then, a worked example, step by step.

00:00:18.040 --> 00:00:19.565
Then, your checklist.

00:00:19.565 --> 00:00:21.727
And finally, a three-question quiz.

00:00:23.028 --> 00:00:27.564
The eight risk surfaces: smart-contract · economic

00:00:27.564 --> 00:00:30.766
· oracle · liquidity · governance ·

00:00:30.766 --> 00:00:35.068
bridge/chain · counterparty · user-operation.

00:00:35.068 --> 00:00:39.478
Score each for likelihood (1–5) × impact (1–5).

00:00:39.478 --> 00:00:42.406
Anything ≥ 15 needs a mitigation or an

00:00:42.406 --> 00:00:45.258
exit; anything ≥ 20 shouldn't be held.

00:00:46.558 --> 00:00:50.272
USDC lending, Protocol Y, Oracle on one

00:00:50.272 --> 00:00:53.430
collateral is thin, 3, 4, 12, Cap

00:00:53.430 --> 00:00:56.794
10%, alert on governance changes.

00:00:56.794 --> 00:01:01.516
LST loop, Rate spike above break-even, 3, 3,

00:01:01.516 --> 00:01:05.699
9, Alert at 4.5% borrow; unwind rule.

00:01:05.699 --> 00:01:09.643
Bridged stablecoin on new L2, Bridge exploit,

00:01:09.643 --> 00:01:12.944
2, 5, 10, Canonical bridge; cap 5%.

00:01:12.944 --> 00:01:16.186
New farm, Contract bug (unaudited upgrade),

00:01:16.186 --> 00:01:17.734
4, 5, 20, Don't hold.

00:01:19.034 --> 00:01:20.494
Here's your checklist.

00:01:20.494 --> 00:01:22.029
Do it now, for real.

00:01:22.029 --> 00:01:26.390
First, Register covers every position and all eight surfaces.

00:01:26.390 --> 00:01:30.145
Next, Scores ≥ 15 have a mitigation or exit.

00:01:30.145 --> 00:01:33.132
And finally, Reviewed monthly and after incidents.

00:01:34.432 --> 00:01:35.642
Question 1.

00:01:35.642 --> 00:01:36.917
How is a risk scored?

00:01:41.337 --> 00:01:44.887
The answer: Likelihood × impact, each 1–5.

00:01:46.187 --> 00:01:47.432
Question 2.

00:01:47.432 --> 00:01:49.257
What's a user-operation risk?

00:01:53.677 --> 00:01:55.915
The answer: Your own mistakes: wrong

00:01:55.915 --> 00:01:57.971
network, bad signature, lost keys.

00:01:59.271 --> 00:02:00.541
Question 3.

00:02:00.541 --> 00:02:01.781
Score 20.

00:02:01.781 --> 00:02:02.416
Action?

00:02:06.836 --> 00:02:08.351
The answer: Don't hold it.

00:02:09.651 --> 00:02:12.166
Do the checklist now, before you move on.

00:02:12.166 --> 00:02:15.601
Next up, Lesson 8.3: The strategy library.
